From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 12:07:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] chore(r61): commit every raw receipt and the wrappers that
 actually produced them

The report cites these by path; a checker cloning the repo needs them present and needs the wrappers to be the versions that ran.

Two wrappers were last committed BEFORE the caret fix, which matters: re-running the committed r61b-gpuB.cmd would have reproduced the caret bug and returned iq4_xs-only rows - the exact silent failure the report documents. Both are now the versions that produced the tables (r61b-gpuB.cmd also in its final B1/B2/B3 form).

Raw rows: the 36 ship-gate perf files, the 8 N7_ROWS perf files, the 4 N7_ROWS deterministic-identity logs, the 12 decode cells, and the re-taken iq3 correctness log. filtercheck.txt/.err are the live validation of the fixed filter before a leg was spent on it - kept as the receipt for that check rather than deleted.

Adds r61-evidence/74-n7id-sha256.txt, which was missing: the four N7_ROWS arms all read sha 9E70CA848F1631D86AD6918B522FA404A3AF076EB87DBDBE83B99BDB39568B02 over 71,778,304 bytes, and that claim is load-bearing in section 2(c). It now has a receipt in the same shape as 44-dump-sha256.txt instead of living only in a transcript.

REPORT CORRECTIONS in the same commit, all tightening claims:

1. The n=7 gain is restated as 22.1x, not 23.8x. unset and N7_ROWS=4 are the same pipeline by construction yet read 497,199 and 461,993 us/run - a 7.6% spread - and 23.8x used the more favourable of the two. The gain is now quoted against the 6-round median of 462,277 from the ship-gate table: ~462,000 -> ~20,900 us/run, 22.1x, cliff 22.5x -> 1.02x. The discrepancy is printed as the precision bound rather than left unexplained. Fixed identically in section 2(c), section 3, the STATUS header and the registry row.

2. The N7_ROWS arms are labelled SINGLE RUNS, and the =2-over-=1 preference is marked a recommendation resting on one comparison, not a measured law.

3. The draft-mtp cells are now supported rather than assumed: identical text would also follow from the flag being ignored, so the report cites the generation rates - 8.5/8.6 t/s against plain 5.5 t/s, the known mtp lift - as evidence the speculative path actually engaged.

4. HQ's 03:24-03:36 activity window is recorded, with the statement that no timed row in any final table was stamped inside it (everything was re-taken on binary 2 at 04:36; perf rows start 10:38).

5. Section 2(a)'s 'byte-for-byte the same module' at NUM_COLS=1 is softened to 'agree in every counted class' - the counts matched, the .spv files were not diffed.

Origin: fork-authored (ArifiLabs lane-249 R61 iq3 MMVQ wide-width, Opus 5 MEDIUM kernel-maker)
Measured-effect: op-level perf-mode only (rows in receipts); served t/s UNMEASURED by the maker - HQ pairs quiet
Lane: lane-249
Cherry-picked-from: 265c6e3a2 (SOURCE PATHS ONLY, ArifiLabs lane-254 R66 integration)
Recut-onto: 1b6185951 (ArifiLabs lane-254 R66c, from ae5a556dd)
